s outweigh the weaknesses.\n\nPlease provide a well-reasoned conclusion based on your analysis, considering the overall impression of the review and the final rating provided by the reviewer.\n\nReview:\n{text}\n\nFinal decision: \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:', '# Task\n"Evaluate the review of the research paper, concentrating on key aspects such as soundness, clarity of presentation, significance of contributions, and identified strengths and weaknesses. Emphasize the reviewer\'s final recommendation and their expressed confidence in their assessment.\n\nWhen determining whether the paper should be classified as suitable for acceptance (Yes) or rejection (No), take into account:\n- The overall tone of the review, including the presence of supportive versus critical comments.\n- The reviewer\'s confidence level, as indicated by their self-assessment and the thoroughness of their critique.\n- The specific rating provided by the reviewer and the rationale behind their decision, including any significant concerns or limitations mentioned.\n\nYour classification should reflect a careful consideration of the reviewer\'s evaluation, particularly in cases where the feedback may suggest an ambiguous or borderline decision." \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:', '# Task\n"Analyze the review of the research paper, focusing on the following criteria: overall soundness, clarity of presentation, significance of contributions, and strengths and weaknesses. Pay special attention to the reviewer\'s final recommendation and their confidence level in their assessment.\n\nFor classifying the paper as suitable for acceptance (Yes) or rejection (No), consider:\n- The balance between positive and negative comments in the review.\n- The tone and language used, which may indicate the reviewer\'s confidence or hesitation.\n- The reviewer\'s rating and specific feedback regarding